# NetBuddy — Cybersecurity Awareness Chatbot (PROG6221 POE)

A WPF desktop application that teaches South African citizens about cybersecurity
through an interactive chatbot. Built incrementally across three parts, culminating
in a task assistant, a quiz mini-game, NLP command recognition, and an activity log.

**Student:** [Your Name] — [Your Student Number]
**Module:** Programming 2A (PROG6221)

---


## Features

**Chatbot (Parts 1 & 2)**
- Voice greeting (WAV) and ASCII art logo
- Personalised greeting using the user's name
- Keyword recognition for cybersecurity topics (passwords, phishing, malware, VPNs, etc.)
- Random responses for variety
- Conversation flow with follow-up handling ("tell me more")
- Memory of the user's name and favourite topic
- Sentiment detection (worried, curious, frustrated, confused)

**Part 3 / POE**
- **Task Assistant** — add, complete and delete cybersecurity tasks, stored in SQL Server LocalDB (full CRUD)
- **Reminders** — set a date *and* time; the app pops up an alert when a reminder is due
- **Quiz Mini-Game** — 12 questions (multiple-choice + true/false), seeded into and loaded from the database, with scoring and feedback
- **NLP Simulation** — understands varied phrasings ("remind me to update my password tomorrow") and routes them to the right feature
- **Activity Log** — records actions with timestamps and updates live; shows recent actions with a "Show More" option
- Separate **Quiz** and **Activity Log** windows

---

## Requirements
- Windows
- .NET 10 SDK
- Visual Studio 2022
- SQL Server LocalDB (installed with Visual Studio)

NuGet packages restore automatically on build:
- `Microsoft.Data.SqlClient`

---

## How to Run
1. Clone the repository.
2. Open `Prog POE Part 2.slnx` in Visual Studio.
3. Make sure SQL Server LocalDB is available (`(localdb)\MSSQLLocalDB`).
4. Press **F5**. On first run the app automatically creates the `netbuddy`
   database, the `tasks` and `quiz_questions` tables, and seeds the quiz questions.
5. Enter your name when prompted, then use the Chat / Tasks tabs and the
   Play Quiz Game / View Activity Log buttons.

No manual database setup is needed — the app creates and seeds everything on launch.

---

## Database
The app uses **SQL Server LocalDB** with Windows Authentication (no password needed).
- `tasks` — id, title, description, reminder_date, is_completed, created_at
- `quiz_questions` — id, question, options, correct_index, explanation, is_true_false

---

## Continuous Integration
GitHub Actions builds the project on every push (restore + build in Release on a Windows runner).

![CI Build Passing](docs/ci-success.png)

---

## Project Structure
- `MainWindow` — chat + tasks UI, reminder pop-ups
- `GameWindow` — quiz window
- `LogWindow` — activity log window
- `Chatbot` — core logic, routes input to the right feature
- `DatabaseService` — LocalDB CRUD + quiz seeding
- `QuizService`, `NlpService`, `ActivityLogService`, `MemoryService`, `SentimentService`, `ResponseService`

